# 🪟 Windows Network Configuration

Windows provides several tools for viewing and troubleshooting network connectivity.

The most important command practiced today was:

```cmd
ipconfig /all
```

This displays detailed network configuration information.

Important information includes:

* IPv4 address
* IPv6 address
* Subnet mask
* Default gateway
* DNS servers
* DHCP status
* Physical/MAC address
* Network adapter information

Example:

```text
IPv4 Address      : 192.168.50.20
Subnet Mask       : 255.255.255.0
Default Gateway   : 192.168.50.1
DNS Server        : 192.168.50.10
```

---

# 🌐 Default Gateway

A default gateway is typically a router or Layer 3 device that forwards traffic from a local network to other networks.

Example:

```text
Windows Client
192.168.50.20
       ↓
Default Gateway
192.168.50.1
       ↓
Other Networks
       ↓
Internet
```

### Interview Definition

> A default gateway is typically a router or Layer 3 device that forwards traffic from a local network to other networks.

---

# 📡 Ping

The `ping` command is used to test network reachability.

Example:

```cmd
ping 127.0.0.1
```

This can test the local TCP/IP stack.

Testing the default gateway:

```cmd
ping 192.168.50.1
```

Testing an external IP:

```cmd
ping 8.8.8.8
```

Testing a hostname:

```cmd
ping google.com
```

---

# 🧠 Understanding Ping Results

Different ping tests provide different information.

### Gateway Test

```cmd
ping <default-gateway>
```

Helps test local network connectivity to the gateway.

### External IP Test

```cmd
ping 8.8.8.8
```

Helps test connectivity to an external IP address.

### Hostname Test

```cmd
ping google.com
```

Tests hostname resolution as part of the process, as well as connectivity to the resolved destination.

